Undo the KConfig escapes when the style reads its config

qtcWriteConfig stores every value through KConfig, which escapes the
backslash, the control characters and a leading or a trailing space.
QtCConfig takes the raw text after the first equals sign and undoes
nothing. A value therefore comes back with its escapes, and the escape
count grows by one level on each save.

An application name that holds a backslash never matches the running
application. The file name of a background image with a backslash never
loads. The dialog shows the escaped text when the user opens it again.

Add unescapeValue and call it on each value of the file. The function
uses the KConfig rules for a value. It reads \\ as the backslash, \s as
a space, \t, \n and \r as the white space characters, and \xNN as a
byte. It keeps an unknown escape as the stored text, so a hand written
path with a single backslash still reads as it stands.

A probe writes each value through KConfig and reads it back with the new
function. It returns 21 of 21 values unchanged, against 9 of 21 before
the change, and three saves of one value give one byte sequence.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 1 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
index 77d60851..ee4c4b59 100644
--- a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
+++ b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
@@ -599,6 +599,72 @@ private:
     QMap<QString, QString> values;
 };
 
+// Convert the stored text of one value to the text the writer gave.
+// The function uses the escape rules of KConfig, the writer of the file, and
+// it keeps an unknown escape as the stored text.
+static QString
+unescapeValue(const QString &val)
+{
+    if(!val.contains('\\'))
+        return val;
+
+    const int len=val.length();
+    QString   res;
+
+    res.reserve(len);
+    for(int i=0; i<len; ++i)
+    {
+        if(val[i]!='\\' || i+1==len)
+        {
+            res+=val[i];
+            continue;
+        }
+
+        const QChar esc(val[++i]);
+
+        switch(esc.unicode())
+        {
+            case 's':
+                res+=' ';
+                break;
+            case 't':
+                res+='\t';
+                break;
+            case 'n':
+                res+='\n';
+                break;
+            case 'r':
+                res+='\r';
+                break;
+            case '\\':
+                res+='\\';
+                break;
+            case 'x':
+            {
+                bool      ok=false;
+                const int code(i+2<len ? val.mid(i+1, 2).toInt(&ok, 16) : 0);
+
+                if(ok && code>=0)
+                {
+                    res+=QChar(char16_t(code));
+                    i+=2;
+                }
+                else
+                {
+                    res+='\\';
+                    res+=esc;
+                }
+                break;
+            }
+            default:
+                res+='\\';
+                res+=esc;
+        }
+    }
+
+    return res;
+}
+
 QtCConfig::QtCConfig(const QString &filename)
 {
     QFile f(filename);
@@ -612,7 +678,7 @@ QtCConfig::QtCConfig(const QString &filename)
             line = stream.readLine();
             int pos=line.indexOf('=');
             if(-1!=pos)
-                values[line.left(pos)]=line.mid(pos+1);
+                values[line.left(pos)]=unescapeValue(line.mid(pos+1));
         }
         f.close();
     }
